      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a monitored setting (3,200 mg/day). The usual maximum for a single dose is 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **Something else**, such as 1,600 mg/day total split differently\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording the intentional above-maximum dose. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
